      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1241955
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-10T17:13:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would like to understand more about the motivation for this.  Based on what I know (and it\u0027s possible I am missing something), I disagree with the underlying premise that this change should be made at all.  This mechanism is meant to capture one, single wakeup reason for every resume or failed suspend (or potentially multiple wakeup IRQs if there are 2+ pending in HW in early resume flow).\n\nIf the kernel actually suspended successfully, we want to capture the IRQ(s) that caused it to resume.\n\nIf the kernel did _not_ suspend successfully, we want to capture the wakeup source (or off-nominal error) that blocked it.\n\nI am not aware of any reason why we would ever want this mechanism to capture both for a single event, and if we did, it would result in incorrect data being provided to the android framework.",
      "revId": "23483f2054c1f9362c5c1eac72874efa20fdd49c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6063c8b0_1ea0bdcf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1723023
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-13T02:06:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason I submit this patch is that kernel would only log wakeup source names even if the suspended system is wakeup by an irq.\n\nConsidering the following cases: a wakeup source is activated during wakeup irq handler\n\nsuspend_enter\n  -\u003e s2idle_loop -\u003e system has suspended\n\n   (wakeup irq interrupt)\n   pm_system_irq_wakeup() -\u003e log_irq_wakeup_reason -\u003e irq handler -\u003e activate wakeup source \n\n   (start resume flow)\n    -\u003e pm_wakeup_pending\n      -\u003e log_suspend_abort_reason\n        -\u003e__log_abort_or_abnormal_wake(true, fmt, args);\n           -\u003e set suspend_abort true\n   ....\n   -\u003e print_wakeup_sources\n      -\u003e only print wakeup source due to suspend_abort is true and irq recorded in log_irq_wakeup_reason is not printed\n\nCould we check wakeup irq first and then check wakeup sources?",
      "parentUuid": "283f8ff2_afc1f316",
      "revId": "23483f2054c1f9362c5c1eac72874efa20fdd49c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    }
